{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak to the children of Israel and let them take for Me a terumah.</b> Say to Israel that I desire that collectors collect a terumah on My behalf. So Moses did when he descended from the mountain, as he said: וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן נִגְּשׁוּ כָּל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, וַיְצַוֵּם אֵת כָּל אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר ה' אִתּוֹ בְּהַר סִינָי (Exodus 34:32), and afterward: וַיֹּאמֶר מֹשֶׁה אֶל כָּל עֲדַת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Exodus 35:4) — these are the Sanhedrin — קְחוּ מֵאִתְּכֶם תְּרוּמָה (Exodus 35:5), and thereby he commanded them to collect. But Israel did not wait for the Sanhedrin to collect; rather, they immediately went out from before Moses and brought beyond sufficiency. Therefore nothing remained for the princes, who had intended to collect besides the stones and the oil that Israel had not yet brought." "<b>From every man.</b> He commanded that they not collect by force, in the manner of those who seize pledges for charity, but that they collect only from volunteers."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:10.531537150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}